<!-- IF level:3,3+ -->
<!-- WHEN TO USE THIS TEMPLATE:
<!-- IF level:3+ -->
Level 3+ (+Govern) is appropriate when:
- High-complexity changes needing review tracking
- Approval workflow with reviewer checkpoints required
- Compliance checkpoints needed
- Stakeholder tracking across multiple workstreams
- Changelog with version history
- Coordinated multi-workstream execution
- Complexity score 80-100
<!-- /IF -->
<!-- IF level:3 -->
Level 3 (+Arch) is appropriate when:
- Changes affect 500+ lines of code
- Architecture decisions need formal documentation (ADRs)
- Executive summary needed for stakeholders
- Risk matrix required
- 4-8 user stories
- Multiple teams or cross-functional work
<!-- /IF -->

<!-- IF level:3+ -->
DO NOT use Level 3+ if:
- Standard complex feature without approval tracking (use Level 3)
- No reviewer checkpoints required (use Level 3)
- Single workstream is sufficient (use Level 3)
<!-- /IF -->
<!-- IF level:3 -->
DO NOT use Level 3 if:
- Simple feature (use Level 1)
- Only verification needed (use Level 2)
- Governance approval workflow required (use Level 3+)
- Compliance checkpoints needed (use Level 3+)
- Multi-agent parallel execution coordination (use Level 3+)
<!-- /IF -->
-->

